- **Invalidation and state integrity:** interaction state referencing a removed node is cleared or retargeted before the node is freed (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:993-1095); element-state changes take a state-only snapshot only when a rule depends on those bits (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:1735-1760; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:784-789); damaged elements mark their ancestor chain (packages/blitz-dom/src/stylo.rs:1346-1350); damage propagates up the DOM and to anonymous ancestors via `layout_parent` (packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/damage.rs:56-195); non-incremental mode marks every node `ALL_DAMAGE` (packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/damage.rs:275-284); damage and dirty flags cleared in one visit per node, skipping clean subtrees (packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/damage.rs:286-331); stale slab ids tolerated by `get`/`contains_key` (packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/damage.rs:296-300; packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/damage.rs:527-530); `dirty_descendants` and `damaged_descendants` ancestor invariants (packages/blitz-dom/src/node/node.rs:614-630; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/node.rs:645-669; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stale_dirty_descendants.rs:5-20; tests/blitz-tests/tests/style_property_invalidation.rs:4-12); new Stylo element data marked `ALL_DAMAGE` (packages/blitz-dom/src/node/stylo_data.rs:100-105); anonymous blocks exist only in `layout_children` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/anonymous_block_cache_invalidation.rs:1-4); every DOM mutation inserts `CONSTRUCT_BOX` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/anonymous_block_cache_invalidation.rs:6-9); geometry memoisation invalidated by a generation counter (packages/blitz-dom/src/tree.rs:36-40; packages/blitz-dom/src/tree.rs:59-73; packages/blitz-dom/src/scrolling.rs:335); animations, transitions and smooth scrolls advance via `resolve(time)` and `is_animating()` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/pseudo_element_update.rs:46-50;
 tests/blitz-tests/tests/fragment_navigation.rs:31-43); a color-scheme change recascades everything (tests/blitz-tests/tests/device_coalescing.rs:94-110); reading the stylist device flushes pending changes (tests/blitz-tests/tests/device_coalescing.rs:80-92); the changed set (§Standard Contracts → Document core) is written at four kinds of site — the 15 mutation-flag sites of `DocumentMutator`, each marking the node whose in-document flag its own condition reads and only when that condition holds (the node itself in `set_node_text`, `append_text_to_node`, `set_attribute`, `clear_attribute`, `set_style_property`, `remove_style_property`, `set_sub_document`, `remove_sub_document`, `set_custom_widget`, `remove_custom_widget`, `remove_node` and `remove_and_drop_node_with`, the parent in `remove_and_drop_all_children` and `add_children_to_parent`, the moved child in `add_children_to_parent`); `snapshot_node_and` when its `ElementState` argument intersects `FOCUS` or `CHECKED`, so a focus move, a checkbox toggle and `toggle_radio` (which marks every radio of the set, changed or not); the `Input` arm of `apply_generated_text_input_event` (a typed character, an IME commit), the last two wherever the node is, in the document or not; and, since 2026-10-13-range-input-interaction, `BaseDocument::apply_range_move`, which marks a range input where a key or a pointerdown changed its value and nothing for a move that changes nothing (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:444-465), and `BaseDocument::apply_select_choice`, which marks a select where a key or typeahead or, on a `multiple` select, a click on a row (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:1013-1054) changed its chosen option or set and nothing for a choice of the chosen option (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:382-408) — and is not written by node creation, hover, active, scroll, a viewport resize, a resource load, an animation or layout, so a `resolve` with nothing written marks nothing in either layout mode;
 the set is engine-touched, a superset of what a snapshot reads as changed (an attribute re-written to itself marks and changes no reading; bounds-only movement changes a reading and marks nothing); ratified by the founder (2026-10-07), the engine half of the item §Document core records (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:1746-1760; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:410-442) — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-change-tracking-and-diff/report.md; under `accessibility` the shell rebuilds the platform accessibility tree on a poll that reported work when the changed set that poll took was non-empty — not on every document change — and takes the set on every such poll with or without the feature; ratified by the founder (2026-10-07), the shell half of the same item, its windowed witness still owed (packages/blitz-shell/src/window.rs:373-391); colour scheme follows the window theme with an override, default Light (packages/blitz-shell/src/window.rs:181-182; packages/blitz-shell/src/window.rs:269-273; packages/blitz-shell/src/window.rs:633-637)
